      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 20 August 2026 — Treble Cone is open, with Home Basin opening at 8:30am and Saddle Basin at 9am. The sun is softening the snow nicely, with Upper Matukituki, Magnum and Upper Skite skiing particularly well this afternoon. Current conditions are 3°C, with winds of 10 km/h and gusts to 18 km/h. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Nine groomed trails are open: Triple Treat, Beginner Platter, Main Street, Upper Skite, Rafill's Run, South Ridge, High Street, Saddle Track and Pete's Treat. Seven of nine terrain areas are open, including Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Matukituki Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Powder Bowl. Motatapu Chutes and Sundance are closed. The NZ Junior Freeride Event is taking place in the upper Saddle from Summit down to Crags, with a managed crossing on High Street. Big Skite is scheduled to open after morning race training. The resort welcomes Wānaka Primary families today. An active road hazard advisory remains in place; roads are chain-free, but all vehicles must carry chains. All three carparks are available.",
